### Parameters
- **src** (str) - Required - The URL or HTML content to embed in the iframe
- **width** (int) - Optional - The width of the iframe in pixels. If not specified, uses the full container width
- **height** (int) - Optional - The height of the iframe in pixels. Default is 600
- **scrolling** (bool) - Optional - Whether to enable scrolling within the iframe. Default is False

### Usage Example
```python
import streamlit as st

# Embed an external website
st.components.v1.iframe(src="https://example.com", width=700, height=500)

# Embed HTML content
html_content = "<h1>Hello World</h1><p>This is embedded HTML</p>"
st.components.v1.iframe(src=html_content, height=300)
```

### Migration Guide
To migrate from `st.components.v1.iframe` to the recommended `st.iframe`:

**Before (Deprecated):**
```python
st.components.v1.iframe(src="https://example.com", width=700, height=500)
```

**After (Recommended):**
```python
st.iframe(src="https://example.com", width=700, height=500)
```

